              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The old `renew` branch in the CLI called ports.Store.Load, ports.Clock() and ports.Store.Save directly and called Tier 2 from Tier 4 presentation, which breaks ARC-BND-02. It is replaced by a Tier 3 use case that goes through `commit`, so the clock and store are reached only through ports. The borrow pre-check that loaded the store in the CLI is also removed. No new effects are added, and the new guards are pure.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 166,
                "quote": "...borrowing is blocked until it is below {money Policy.blockingBalance}"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The 5.00 threshold now lives only in Policy.blockingBalance. The deleted CLI literal `5.00m` and the duplicated fines-minus-payments sum were a second definition, so this change removes drift risk. The error messages and Accounts.isBlocked both reference the Policy value. The `>= Policy.blockingBalance` comparison appears in both isBlocked and ensureNotBlocked, but the two agree and sit in the same Tier 2 module. This is a minor restatement that I did not penalise.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
